@@ -90,3 +90,9 @@ Caching never replaces live CI, publication checks, reconciliation or final comp
 ## Structured resume packet
 
 `resume --run RUN --spec CURRENT_SPEC.json` reads one locked snapshot containing retained budgets, progress references, task captures, validated evidence references, native handles when retained, and PR-wide unfinished claims. Repeat `--spec` for known current tasks. Current specs use ordinary freshness checks; an omitted governing spec remains explicitly missing and never implies reusable coverage. Missing or damaged original evidence remains explicit. Read the referenced original results and progress before assessing findings or exact acceptances. The packet makes no mutations, infers no governing inputs and never authorizes recovery or publication. Reconcile unfinished native/domain work and obtain the existing recovery authority before using ordinary recovery commands.
+
+## Private CI observer receipt
+
+The existing waiter supports `python3 PLUGIN_ROOT/runtime/dk-ci/scripts/ci_wait.py --pr PR_URL --head FULL_SHA --receipt`. Pending progress and the terminal JSON include `observer_receipt`, a private state path plus `/current/receipt` pointer. The receipt retains canonical PR/head identity, observation id, original deadline, current owner/state, last observation and complete final policy evidence. It shares the existing atomic observer state and lock; classification and final evidence remain under that lock.
+
+Interrupting and resuming the ordinary waiter retains its original window. A retained receipt keeps updating on resume even if the flag is omitted. Beginning a new observation clears the prior terminal credential and requires live checks; a saved success never authorizes readiness, recovery, reruns or publication. Check the receipt identity against the requested head. Denied access remains latched until repaired and explicitly retried. Head changes, failures, timeout, absent checks and helper errors remain unsuccessful outcomes. This adds bookkeeping only; the waiter never launches or reruns CI jobs.
